 that they could come back and  during an interview with variety michael  waldron was asked if wanda actually died  or not in which he replied i think  that's up for interpretation she made  some kind of sacrificial act that  destroyed the darkhold in every universe  which is protecting wanda and every  universe from being seduced by the  darkhold whether she's dead or not  remains to be seen i know what it's like  to love characters and to not want them  to be gone and to hate when they do bad  things but that's part of the fun of  watching stuff and getting swept up in  it now here's the deal if you actually  think wanda's dead i'm gonna go ahead  and say she's not typically when marvel  characters die specifically main mcu  avengers characters they're pretty clear  that they die also the actors and  actresses typically talk about what  their time was like playing that  superhero how they're gonna miss that  time how it was a dream come true and  how they're going to always reflect back  on and be super happy about what they  did as that character and how it was  just time to move on this is what  happened with robert downing jr's iron  man chris evans as captain america and  noticed that the characters who are  still around that never really discussed  their fate or future of the character  have all decided to come back mark  ruffalo is back as the hulk in she-hulk  chris hemsworth of course is back as  thor and thor love and thunder basically  when an actor is done being a character  we know and here's the deal elizabeth  olsen has actually been talking about  the future of the scarlet witch recently  and not many people remember this but  kevin feige actually specifically stated  about a year ago that doctor strange and  the multiverse of madness will not be  the last place we see wanda in an  interview with deadline they were  talking about one division and they  asked marvel studios president kevin  feige if there would be an evolution of  wanda storyline through other properties  in which he replied yes to an evolution  of storyline probably and inevitably in  many different capacities and this was  an obvious reference to doctor strange  and the multiverse madness because this  was a year before it came out but check  this out he then went on to say  referring again to doctor strange and  the multiverse of madness he said that's  the first place where that story will  continue but  there will be other places so this was  almost a full year ago in an interview  with deadline and this is the marvel  studios president telling us that  there's going to be other places where  the scarlet witch's story is continued  so it looks like not only is the scarlet  witch not done but the story for her  might have already been planned out and  this actually makes me wonder if they  have planned a one division season two  because something that struck me as  rather odd about multiverse of madness  is that there was not much mention of  vision and we never even saw him not  even in a flashback i don't think there  were any pictures of him i think they  mentioned his name maybe one time when  she said viz and they referred to him in  other times but he really was not a part  of this movie it was all about her kids  but don't forget white vision is out  there somewhere we have no idea what  happened to him we have no idea what his  future story is but maybe that's where  one division two comes into place the  first season was a huge success it would  make sense that they would do another  one and kevin feige pretty much a year  ago was already talking about wanda's  story popping up in other places after  multiverse of madness so you never know  now in recent interviews people of  course are asking elizabeth olson what's  next and every time she talks about this  she makes no mention that she is done as  the character in fact she says that she  is pretty excited to continue to play  the character and excited to see what  stories could come along for her but it  looks like she might have somewhat of an  idea of what could be next for the  scarlet witch here's what she had to say  in an interview with fandango if there's  a good idea i'm happy to play her i also  think her being old will actually be  kind of amazing in the comics her power  kind of deteriorates her and ages her in  a way in some of the comics i do think  of that as being kind of amazing i kind  of imagined myself one day with like  prosthetics and silver hair and like  playing her as this like older wise  woman and so i do have this kind of this  dream of aging her quite a bit i just  really think she's ancient in her like  the myth of the scarlet witch is this  ancient myth and so that's something  that i kind of adore about a potential  future that i'm just kind of throwing  out and i really don't know where it  would go that would be an interesting  storyline but fortunately for us and  maybe unfortunately for elizabeth olsen  i think she's going to be returning  before then especially if you consider  the rumors about her signing a deal with  marvel for multiple more projects this  will most likely include her own solo  feature but will also most likely  include her teaming up with some other  people as well now i don't think that  she'll be playing an avenger anytime  soon because i'm pretty sure doctor  strange is going to have a part of the  avengers right now also wong seems to be  a pretty prominent member of the mc  right now he's been showing up  everywhere and we just got confirmation  that he's going to be appearing in  she-hulk he might have a little bit of a  problem with wanda being a part of the  avengers he was just kind of tortured by  her and plus not to mention his  girlfriend died trying to kill the  darkhold and she killed a lot of a  student so i'm thinking wong's not okay  with her being an avenger however the  darker side of the mcu right now is  being established and definitely the  mystic side is coming out we have moon  knight we have blade coming up and  multiverse of madness truly had a darker  tone to it ghost rider was supposed to  appear in multiverse madness but that  scene was cut and we have the black  knight coming so hopefully the midnight  suns are being set up and hopefully  wanda can be a part of the midnight suns  plus not to mention at the end of doctor  strange 2 in the post credit cleo was  introduced and she says that doctor  strange caused an incursion well wanda  is a nexus being a reality warping being  and it looks like she somehow has  managed to communicate across the  multiverse as she was able to destroy  the darkhold in every different universe  she could always come back to actually  help doctor strange kind of do damage  control on what she caused because let's  face it the only reason doctor strange  had the multiverse jump was because of  the scarlet witch so it is kind of all  her fault so i definitely think there's  potential for her to return in doctor  strange iii however i do think she is  going to eventually get her own solo  movie not her and doctor strange or her  in another character but her own solo  movie and this could be about the  relationship between her and her father  at one point in time in the comics who  is magneto once you get the x-men and  mutants rolling into the mcu this could  be an incredible storyline magneto finds  out how powerful she is and he wants to  go and recruit her for his team but then  of course you would have professor x who  would try to stop magneto and get her to  join him kind of similar to x-men the  final stand with the phoenix force  instead it's the scarlet witch i'm also  excited for the fact that we could be  getting a one division season two there  has been absolutely no confirmation  about this whatsoever yet but the way  kevin feige talked about her story in  continuing after doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness leads me to  believe that they do have plans for her  and right now marvel shows are getting  continuations what if season 2 is coming  and actually loki season 2 is about to  start filming it would make sense that  wanda would get a season two of one  division it might not be called one  division but it's very clear that there  is a lot more of wanda story left  specifically what did happen with that  other vision it looks like we are  eventually going to find out as it looks  like the scarlet witch is not done in  the mcu and elizabeth olsen will be  returning to play her so let me know  what you would like to see as far as the  story is concerned for the scarlet witch  in the mcu let me know your thoughts in  the comments down below don't forget to  like the video and subscribe so you  don't miss out on any of the latest news  for live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter and as always  thank you all so much for watching woof  me

